1
00:00:22,117 --> 00:00:24,507
This is Kamikoani Village in Akita Prefecture.

2
00:00:24,507 --> 00:00:29,090
Its population was 2,063 in the 2020 census.

3
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:37,059
The village stretches about 33 kilometers north
to south, but mountains cover most of it.

4
00:00:37,059 --> 00:00:42,837
Let’s look at where people live and work.

5
00:00:44,937 --> 00:00:50,754
Village documents classify 92.7% of
the land as forest and wilderness.

6
00:00:50,754 --> 00:00:55,970
Flat land and settlements lie along
the Koani River and its tributaries.

7
00:00:55,970 --> 00:01:05,198
Snow covers the village for about a third of the year,
reaching two meters in southern and eastern mountain areas.

8
00:01:05,198 --> 00:01:11,417
Despite its size, land available
for homes and farming is limited.

9
00:01:13,517 --> 00:01:18,134
We now look at population by census small area.

10
00:01:18,134 --> 00:01:21,213
The map divides the village into ten districts.

11
00:01:21,213 --> 00:01:24,291
Darker green means a larger population.

12
00:01:24,291 --> 00:01:32,179
The color covers each entire district; green
mountains are not necessarily residential areas.

13
00:01:32,179 --> 00:01:36,797
Actual settlements are smaller and more
scattered than these boundaries suggest.

14
00:01:38,897 --> 00:01:45,109
In 2020, Okitaomote had the
largest population, at 741.

15
00:01:45,109 --> 00:01:52,702
Kosawada had 309; together, these two districts
held about half the village’s population.

16
00:01:52,702 --> 00:02:00,295
In 2000, Okitaomote had 1,245
residents and Kosawada had 437.

17
00:02:00,295 --> 00:02:04,897
Even the larger districts
continue to lose population.

18
00:02:06,997 --> 00:02:10,891
The rate of decline varies by district.

19
00:02:10,891 --> 00:02:19,112
Minamizawa fell from 72 residents in 2000
to 23 in 2020, a drop of roughly 70%.

20
00:02:19,112 --> 00:02:25,386
Fukudate fell from 221 to
179, a decline of about 20%.

21
00:02:25,386 --> 00:02:31,877
Both are shrinking, but at different speeds.

22
00:02:33,977 --> 00:02:38,424
Forestry historically supported
this mountainous village.

23
00:02:38,424 --> 00:02:44,429
Village records show 536 forestry workers in 1975.

24
00:02:44,429 --> 00:02:51,323
That fell to 85 in 2000 and 35 in 2015.

25
00:02:51,323 --> 00:03:03,332
Most worked in national-forest-related jobs; the village cites restructuring
and a prolonged timber-industry slump linked to imported wood.

26
00:03:03,332 --> 00:03:09,337
The forests remain, but far
fewer people work in them.

27
00:03:11,437 --> 00:03:18,264
Farming centers on rice grown on limited flat
land, with buckwheat and soybeans also cultivated.

28
00:03:18,264 --> 00:03:27,557
A fiscal 2024 document says the farmers taking
over land have already reached their capacity.

29
00:03:27,557 --> 00:03:33,815
Their fields remain scattered, rather
than consolidated into efficient blocks.

30
00:03:33,815 --> 00:03:38,557
Mountain terrain and winter
snow removal add to the burden.

31
00:03:40,657 --> 00:03:42,703
There is manufacturing, too.

32
00:03:42,703 --> 00:03:56,343
Nihon Kikai Kogyo’s San-i plant in Obayashi, attracted by the prefecture
in 1987, is listed as handling snow fences and multistory parking systems.

33
00:03:56,343 --> 00:04:08,392
Akita’s 2021 manufacturing tabulation lists four village establishments—in
food, wood, furniture and metal—with 41 workers in total.

34
00:04:08,392 --> 00:04:16,577
This covers qualifying establishments, including those with
at least four workers, and excludes sole proprietorships.

35
00:04:18,677 --> 00:04:23,438
This chart shows the jobs of
people living in the village.

36
00:04:23,438 --> 00:04:32,054
Employed residents fell from
1,494 in 2000 to 876 in 2020.

37
00:04:32,054 --> 00:04:42,938
Manufacturing fell from 351 to 128, while agriculture,
forestry, fishing and mining combined fell from 260 to 117.

38
00:04:42,938 --> 00:04:49,513
In 2020, health care and welfare was
the largest category, with 216 workers.

39
00:04:49,513 --> 00:04:59,717
These are important jobs, but worker counts alone do not
show what the village sells to earn income from outside.

40
00:05:01,817 --> 00:05:07,723
This chart includes residents
who work outside the village.

41
00:05:07,723 --> 00:05:19,317
In 2020, 313 of its 876 employed residents—about
36%—commuted to other municipalities.

42
00:05:19,317 --> 00:05:24,130
Another 191 people commuted into Kamikoani.

43
00:05:24,130 --> 00:05:30,911
The jobs supporting village life extend
beyond its administrative boundaries.

44
00:05:30,911 --> 00:05:40,537
The 128 residents in manufacturing and the 41 workers in
qualifying local factories measure different populations.

45
00:05:42,637 --> 00:05:47,571
Let’s move through the population
figures in five-year steps from 2000.

46
00:05:47,571 --> 00:05:54,650
The total fell from 3,369 to
2,063, a decline of nearly 40%.

47
00:05:54,650 --> 00:06:01,515
Residents aged 65 and over also
fell, from 1,197 to 1,107.

48
00:06:01,515 --> 00:06:08,808
But children under 15 fell much
more sharply, from 363 to 117.

49
00:06:08,808 --> 00:06:16,317
Even with fewer older residents, their
share of the total population rises.

50
00:06:18,417 --> 00:06:25,886
In 2020, about 54% of residents
were aged 65 or over.

51
00:06:25,886 --> 00:06:35,779
The village’s population strategy identifies net outmigration in the late
teens and early twenties, when people enter education or employment.

52
00:06:35,779 --> 00:06:42,844
Its newsletter reports three
births and 51 deaths in 2025.

53
00:06:42,844 --> 00:06:52,737
Alongside people leaving for work, deaths
exceeding births contribute to population decline.

54
00:06:54,837 --> 00:07:02,916
Kamikoani’s scattered settlements have
sustained life amid mountains and snow.

55
00:07:02,916 --> 00:07:10,374
The loss of national-forest-related jobs
is a change shared by forestry villages.

56
00:07:10,374 --> 00:07:16,174
Young people leaving and deaths exceeding
births also affect many depopulating areas.

57
00:07:16,174 --> 00:07:25,703
Here, farming on limited land, small-scale manufacturing
and commuting outside the village help sustain livelihoods.

58
00:07:25,703 --> 00:07:34,197
As population falls, maintaining homes, settlements and
the roads connecting them becomes a central challenge.
